Repair the AI-assisted port's three defects against CMS's FY2021.0 COBOL pricer.

Applied by sides/port_runner.py to a build copy of rcaran/hospice-cms-pricer-java @ 6558476
(one squashed commit dated 2026-06-05), which has no licence file and is never committed to this
repository. The port is unchanged apart from the three points below; nothing else is touched.

1 and 2. FullPricerStrategy.java:79-86. A continuous-home-care line of less than 32 units is one
   CHC day, paid at the routine-home-care rate for that day. The COBOL paragraph
   2021-V210-CHC-0652 computes WRK-PAY-RATE2 and nothing else: HOSPR210.cbl:6409-6411 and :6418-6420
   for a day of less than 32 units, :6430-6434 for 32 or more. The port also sets the two flags and
   increments the two counters that say the claim carries routine home care days. Only the RHC
   paragraphs write those: BILL-HIGH-RHC-DAYS at HOSPR210.cbl:6036, BILL-LOW-RHC-DAYS at :5997, the
   indicators RHC-HIGH-DAY-IND at :6055 and RHC-LOW-DAY-IND at :6018, and the return code
   73/74/75/77 is assigned from the indicators alone in V210-SUM-RHC-0651-RATE (:6274-6312). So a
   claim billing nothing but a short CHC line comes back from the COBOL with 00, no high day and no
   low day. Four statements are removed: the two counters (the day counts) and the two flags (the
   return code).

3. PaymentCalculator.java:81. The COBOL computes

       COMPUTE WRK-PAY-RATE2 ROUNDED =
           (((2021-V210-CHC-LS-RATE * BILL-BENE-WAGE-INDEX) +
             2021-V210-CHC-NLS-RATE) / 24) * (BILL-UNITS2 / 4)

   (HOSPR210.cbl:6430-6434) into a PIC 9(06)V9(02) field (HOSPR210.cbl:207). The ROUNDED phrase
   applies to the store, not to the two divisions inside it, and IBM's rule is that a result with
   more decimal places than the receiving field is truncated unless the statement that produces it
   says ROUNDED (https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/cobol-zos/6.3.0?topic=operations-rounded-phrase), so the
   hourly rate is truncated. The port rounded it half-up at ten places, which puts a claim a cent
   over whenever the exact product lands on a half. Truncating at four places is what reproduces the
   COBOL on all 5,000 claims of this case, and it is where CMS's own Java migration truncates the
   same rate (ApplyContinuousHomeCareRateWithoutQualityReduction.java:85, RoundingMode.DOWN at four
   decimal places), which agrees with the COBOL on every continuous-home-care line.

   Example, claim C00408 (76 units, wage index 1.3689): the exact product is 1421.425679, the COBOL
   writes 1421.42, the port as published wrote 1421.43.

